1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. Bb5 (3. f4 g6 4. Nf3 Bg7 5. Bc4 (5. Bb5 Nd4! 6. O-O Nh6! $15 { [%csl Gg8,Ba6,Bb5,Bb7,Bf5][%cal Ge8g8,Ba7a6,Bb7b5,Bc8b7,Be7e6,Gf4f5,Be6f5,Bh6f5] }) 5... e6 { [%csl Bd5,Be7][%cal Bg8e7,Bd7d5] } 6. O-O (6. f5?! Nge7 7. fxe6 dxe6 8. d3 h6 9. O-O g5!? $10 { [%csl Bg8,Gf4,Be5][%cal Be8g8,Gg6f4,Ge7g6,Bc6e5,Gg6e5] }) 6... Nge7 7. d3 (7. Qe1 { [%csl Be8][%cal Be1e8] } 7... O-O 8. d3 d5! $15) 7... d5! $15) (3. g3 g6 4. Bg2 Bg7 5. d3 d6 { [%csl Be5,Ge7][%cal Be7e5,Gg8e7] } 6. Be3 (6. f4 e6! { [%csl Be7,Bf5][%cal Bg8e7,Gf4f5,Be6f5,Be7f5] } 7. Nf3 Nge7 8. O-O O-O 9. Be3) 6... e5 (6... Rb8 7. Qd2 b5) (6... e6 7. Qd2) 7. Qd2 Nge7 8. Bh6 (8. f4 O-O 9. Nf3 Nd4! $10) 8... Bxh6 9. Qxh6 Nd4! $15 { [%csl Be6,Gd5,Bb6,Gb4][%cal Bc8e6,Bd8b6,Gd6d5,Gb7b5,Gb5b4] }) 3... g6!? { This move is thought to be inaccurate, but in reality I think black gets a really easy game and if white wants to get the +0.3, then he must be extremely accurate. Most notably, white won't get typical king's side attack.
This idea was introduced to me by Naroditsky } 4. Bxc6 bxc6 5. d3 Bg7 6. f4 { [%csl Bc4][%cal Bc5c4] } 6... d6 7. Nf3 Nh6!? { [%csl Bf6,Be5,Bf7][%cal Bf7f6,Be7e5,Bh6f7] } 8. O-O O-O 9. Qe1 f6! 10. b3 (10. Qh4 Nf7 { [%csl Be5,Bf5][%cal Be7e5,Bf6f5] } 11. g4 { [%csl Ge5,Gf5][%cal Ge7e5,Gf4f5] } 11... e6 12. Bd2 f5! $10 { [%csl Gc4,Gg1,Gb2][%cal Gc5c4,Gd8b6,Gb6g1,Gb6b2] }) (10. Be3 e5 11. fxe5 fxe5 12. h3 { [%csl Bg4][%cal Bh6g4] } 12... Nf7! $10 { [%csl Ge6,Bc4,Gb2][%cal Gc8e6,Bc5c4,Ga8b8,Gb8b2] }) 10... e5 11. fxe5 fxe5 12. Bg5 Qa5! $10 { [%csl Be7,Be8,Gd6][%cal Bg5e7,Bf8e8,Gh6f7,Gf7d6] } *


