1. e4 c5 { Here, I will recommend you many e6 set-ups as I believe they are the best way to counter many gambits. There are alternative and if you want to, you can look into them but I hope you will like my recommendations } 2. d4 (2. b4 cxb4 3. a3 e6! { Sound and in spirit of my favourite sicilian - kan. We get a scheveningen pawn structure here. } 4. axb4 Bxb4 5. Bb2!? { tricky move } (5. c3 Be7 6. d4 (6. Qg4 g6!? { If you've never played the Kan Sicilian this may look wierd to you, but it's actually quite a good line and idea. We often play move g6 in scheveningen pawn structures as it prevents various f5 ideas. If they ever play Bh6 to prevent us from castling we always have Bf8! } { [%csl Bf6,Bd6][%cal Bg8f6,Bd7d6] } 7. d4 Nf6! $15 { And black is doing fine here. We have quite similar plan to the mainline } { [%csl Gd6,Gc6,Ge5,Bg8][%cal Gd7d6,Gb8c6,Ge6e5,Be8g8] }) 6... d6 7. Bd3 Nf6! { and we just play the hedgehog, but white cannot really defend well against d5 break. } { [%csl Gb6,Gb7,Gd7,Bg8][%cal Gb7b6,Gc8b7,Gb8d7,Be8g8] } 8. f4 e5! $15 { Nice motif to know. We can strike with quick e5 as white isn't developed. If they "win" a pawn then Ng4 and nc6 in the end is quite strong. If they don't take, then exd4 cxd4 d5! creating outpost on e4, } { [%csl Bd4,Be4][%cal Gf4e5,Gd6e5,Gd4e5,Gf6g4,Gg4e5,Be5d4,Bc3d4,Bd6d5,Bf6e4,Bd5e4] }) 5... Bf8! { The best move is Nf6, but this is also quite decent and I think it is just easier to play } 6. Nf3 d6 7. d4 Nf6 8. Bd3 { This is the most thematic plan for white. People have tried different set-ups but our typical kan is good enough there } 8... Be7 9. O-O O-O 10. c4 Nc6! { And we play idea quite common in King's Indian Defence. It will be clear in a moment. On the sidenote, Nb4 is also possible and quite potent. } { [%csl Gd4,Ge5,Bb4][%cal Gc6d4,Ge6e5,Bc6b4] } 11. Nc3 e5! $15 { We create an outpost on d4. We may continue with Bg4 and just trade pieces and go for the endgame. Here, Black just needs to liquidate and white must think how to prove that they can hold it. } { [%csl Gd4,Bg4][%cal Gc6d4,Ge5d4,Bc8g4] }) (2. a3 e6 { If they play anything else than b4, then it is something we've already look at, but with a3 included, so white just wasted a tempo more or less. } 3. b4 cxb4 4. axb4 Bxb4! { Transposes into wing gambit }) 2... cxd4 3. c3 Nf6! 4. Bd3?! dxc3 5. Nxc3 Nc6 6. Nf3 d6! $17 { [%csl Bg6,Bg7,Bg8,Gd7][%cal Bg7g6,Bf8g7,Be8g8,Gc8d7] } *


